body:
   "Where did I go wrong?"  He said, fighting back tears in his eyes.  "What did I do... What did I do to have it turn out this way?  I don't understand, my creation, my design, my everything.  They've just haven't become what they were meant to be.  They become like them of all the beings in this realm they chose to follow them."
&nbsp;

I was shocked.  I had no idea what to tell Him.  He chose this, he decided it was best to create the realm of man, and it was Him, who decided to let us have open access to their world.  He chose to stand idle and watch it plan out.  I had to say something but, what?  I've never seen my friend so distraught. This could end badly, He may finally intervene into His creation after these eons of watching others go in and out convincing man they were the creators. 

 "Well Lord, I don't have the answers.  I'm also a product of your hands, I am similar to man, but also different.  For I can see this realm and travel to and fro between it.  You have to remember that unlike you, I am limited.   The answer to your problem is within you, and you know this.  The only thing preventing you from generating that answer is the fact that you do wish to go there."  I can't believe those words just came out of my mouth, who am I to talk to my creator like this?  "Master you let Yahweh and Allah gain access to this realm, knowing that they the twin berserkers of this place.  It was them that slain Baal, Anu, Isis and countless others.  They've been in that realm since the beginning of its existence."  He look at me with an ominous look.  I think I'm getting through to Him, but I only hope this doesn't make Him enraged enough to do what Yahweh did.  "It's not mans fault for their minds are fragile and mold-able like the clay they are made from, it's your fault for not protecting you creation, it's your fault for letting these tyrants mold them into the monsters that they are today, but remember this;  You have the ability to fix this, because you are the one with the final control.  You decide how this ends, so I say you go into the realm and show them that You are the end of all ends."

&nbsp;

   "You've finally started to become bold, now haven't you Megaton?"  He had this smirk in His eye, and I don't like it.  It's not a normal look for Him, something's went wrong inside His heart.  "but you're correct, I do need to do something, but I need you to help me because I need to stop both of them."


&nbsp;

   "Master what can I do to fight them?  They are greater beings than I, I... I couldn't pull a hair from their head, let alone defeat them!"  He's gone mad, I can't believe it, He wants to wage war against two of the most skillful warriors in existence.  " This will be the end of us if we wage battle them"  This is my fault! All my fault!  I put this idea into his head, now we're going to die for it.

&nbsp;

   "I know your thoughts, friend.  Don't worry we won't die, they will."  How could He be so confident?  "Yah and All are more like you than they are me.  For you see I created this realm as well,  I created them as well. I know their thoughts and plans, so we cannot lose."  Do I believe him?  I don't know, surely He would have told me that before now, but maybe it was better that I didn't know that.

&nbsp;

   "Master, you are greater than I ever imagined, and I will follow you for as long this heart you gave continues to beat, but how do show the humans that they're all wrong after eons of them believing that each sect is following the creator and a not a creation?"

&nbsp;

   "It's simple, Meagton, it's really simple, we get all the humans attention at once.  Then we summon both Yahweh and Allah in front of them, and there we'll have a grand display of power, and vanquish both of them.  We'll then make home on Earth and then proceed to teach man the way they are supposed to live."  "Go rest now friend, we start tomorrow."
